{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Disjunctive Normal Form.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Disjunctive Normal Form.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"disjunctive normal form disjunctive normal form","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Disjunctive Normal Form.md","fileName":"Disjunctive Normal Form.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Disjunctive Normal Form","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 22:54\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Formal Logic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Formal Logic","Truth Table","Electronic Circuits","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Disjunctive Normal Form.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Disjunctive Normal Form.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"disjunctive normal form disjunctive normal form","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Disjunctive Normal Form.md","fileName":"Disjunctive Normal Form.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Disjunctive Normal Form","heading":"Disjunctive Normal Form","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A proposition is in disjunctive normal form when it is an OR of AND clauses whose terms are variables or negated variables. Each true row of a [[Truth Table]] supplies one conjunction: use the variable when the row assigns true and its negation when the row assigns false.\n\nTaking the disjunction of these row clauses produces a formula with exactly the table's output behavior. This construction shows that AND, OR, and NOT gates can implement any Boolean input-output table used by a [[Electronic Circuits|combinatorial logic circuit]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Formal Logic","Truth Table","Electronic Circuits","FoundationsOfComputation_2.3.2.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Disjunctive Normal Form.md::2","sourceKey"